<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Harper, Liberia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Harper is a port town in south-eastern Liberia on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-palmas">Cape Palmas</a>, the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maryland-county">Maryland County</a>. It was founded in 1834 by settlers sent by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maryland-state-colonization-society">Maryland State Colonization Society</a> and named after Robert Goodloe Harper, a supporter of the colonisation movement. It was the capital of the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maryland">Maryland</a> until that state joined Liberia in 1857.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/harper-liberia.jpg" alt="Harper, Liberia" width="320" height="362" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Global Photographer · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HarperLiberia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
